Body:
CodeNomad's bounded V2 transcript integration has a concrete correctness case for this revision token.

On the current beta message surface:

- `packages/server/src/handlers/message.ts` encodes a pagination cursor as `{ id, order, direction }`;
- `Session.messages` resolves that message ID to its current `session_message.seq` when the cursor is consumed;
- `session.compaction.started` appends a new `compaction` projection at a new sequence, while compaction deltas/end update that same row;
- `session.revert.committed` can delete the row referenced by an older cursor. A missing cursor anchor currently returns `[]`, which is indistinguishable from a valid transcript edge.

This means a bounded client can hold a structurally valid cursor while its previously observed end, total, or search rank is no longer authoritative. Compaction exposes this systematically because it advances the transcript end without a new user prompt.

We opened #44660 for optional `seek` plus `cursor.range.{start,end,total}`. That positional metadata needs to compose with the revision requested here:

- each message-list response should identify the transcript revision used for both `data` and range metadata;
- the revision should change on append, in-place message content replacement, and removal;
- clients should be able to distinguish a stale/deleted cursor anchor from a genuine empty edge;
- search results should carry the same revision if server-side transcript search is added later.

This keeps responsibilities separate: #44660 supplies position/random access; #43766 supplies snapshot authority.
